[h1]Speculative Markets - Morgenroete Compatibility[/h1]
Adds Morgenroete's musical instruments, uranium and printed publications to Speculative Markets. These goods get investor interest, booms and crashes, bank exposure, industry interventions and Finance-panel entries.

[b]Requires Speculative Markets 1.0.5 (or matching 1.0.5-beta.1) and Morgenroete 2.9.0e Curie, on Victoria 3 1.15.1.[/b]

[h2]Load order[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385002128]Community Mod Framework[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2889925770]Morgenroete - Dawn of Flavor[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3831434383]Speculative Markets[/url] OR [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275304]Speculative Markets - Beta[/url]
[*]This Morgenroete compatibility patch
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275348]Speculative Markets - CMF Compatibility[/url]
[/list]
Enable exactly one Speculative Markets channel. Set this order manually.

[b]Disable the older third-party Speculative Markets+Morgenroete patch.[/b] This replaces that bridge; do not run both. Keep a copy of your save before changing mods.

[h2]What changes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Integrates the three goods and their industries with the current Speculative Markets systems.
[*]Keeps the current Finance window and all 52 tracked goods, including electricity.
[*]Adds the instrument workshop throughput modifier needed for investor effects.
[/list]
Air travel and orchestral music are outside this patch's scope. No base-game balance settings are changed.

This patch must be updated when either parent changes the definitions it uses. It does not promise compatibility with every additional mod or old save. Please include your versions, load order and error log in bug reports.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Morgenroete's goods, buildings and artwork belong to its authors. This is a separate compatibility patch maintained alongside Speculative Markets.

